1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,889
In July 1931, the governor of Oklahoma

2
00:00:03,899 --> 00:00:05,983
declared martial law over a bridge south

3
00:00:05,993 --> 00:00:06,619
of Durant.

4
00:00:06,849 --> 00:00:08,525
Then he showed up wearing a pistol.

5
00:00:09,075 --> 00:00:11,265
A new free bridge over the Red River,

6
00:00:11,275 --> 00:00:13,882
linking Durant and Denison, Texas, was

7
00:00:13,892 --> 00:00:14,432
finished.

8
00:00:14,662 --> 00:00:16,649
But the owners of the old toll bridge got

9
00:00:16,659 --> 00:00:18,957
a federal court order to keep it closed.

10
00:00:19,407 --> 00:00:21,867
Texas barricaded its end, and Texas

11
00:00:21,877 --> 00:00:23,354
Rangers were sent to guard it.

12
00:00:23,904 --> 00:00:26,894
Oklahoma's governor, Alfalfa Bill Murray,

13
00:00:26,904 --> 00:00:29,308
had the barricades torn down, and later

14
00:00:29,318 --> 00:00:30,671
called out the National Guard.

15
00:00:31,121 --> 00:00:33,131
They called it the Red River Bridge War.

16
00:00:33,361 --> 00:00:34,421
No one was hurt.

17
00:00:35,071 --> 00:00:37,360
The free bridge officially opened on Labor

18
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:40,684
Day, 1931, and carried traffic until the

19
00:00:40,694 --> 00:00:41,618
1990s.

20
00:00:42,068 --> 00:00:44,050
A piece of it still sits in the city park

21
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:45,593
in Colbert, Oklahoma.

22
00:00:46,043 --> 00:00:48,086
Comment your town, and it could be next.

